      "content": "that's a pretty clear-cut way to put it. but i'm hearing a lot of debate about how \"marginalized communities\" or \"dehumanizing tropes\" are defined. some people argue that if we let platforms decide that, it basically just becomes a way to censor any political parody that's uncomfortable or critical of certain social movements. isn't there a risk that following this \"standard\" just leads to over-moderation of legitimate political speech?",
